WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.968
Anika: Okay, connection reuse could avoid repeated handshakes. Our client currently opens many short connections.

2
00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:15.048
Lukas: What closes them, client policy or server? Reuse won't help if the server closes first.

3
00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:22.103
Anika: Client pooling is disabled for this integration. The server supports bounded persistent connections.

4
00:00:22.103 --> 00:00:29.567
Hannah: So round-trip time remains, but setup shrinks. That isn't a shorter network route.

5
00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:37.007
Priya: Just to confirm, test stale connections too, right? Idle timeouts could change the outcome.

6
00:00:37.007 --> 00:00:44.831
Raj: Yes, align pool expiry below server timeout. Add jitter to avoid synchronized reconnect bursts.

7
00:00:44.831 --> 00:00:51.743
Lukas: And cap concurrency rather than growing indefinitely. Queue delay belongs in the measurements too.

8
00:00:51.743 --> 00:00:57.142
Anika: I'm on it for those client limits. We'll keep an eye on pool waits.

9
00:00:57.142 --> 00:01:05.806
Hannah: If we're seeing connection resets during tests, compare idle age. Avoid blind payment retries.

10
00:01:05.806 --> 00:01:13.870
Priya: So, sandbox calls first, roughly current concurrency. Production adoption still needs a separate review.

